  "force_reason": "Groups are book_quote, not market_state+book_flow: the 7 depth columns cannot exist before 2026-08-25 because the venue serves no historical order book, and under --complete-cases they pin training to the live era; the 4 quote columns are recoverable to 2025-12-10 from the venue's own candles. implied_vol is out for the SAME reason and it was missed: its 5 columns are dense only from 2026-09, when the live recorder started, and the ladder_candles backfill before that covers 2-3% of the candle rows. Under --complete-cases those 5 columns cost 38,586 training rows and 20,013 evaluated windows (61,379 -> 41,366) while adding 303 windows worth of nothing, which pins training to the live era exactly as the depth columns did. It goes back in when backfill_implied_vol has run over the full range -- the candle fits score r2 0.97-0.98, so the data is recoverable, it has simply not been built. PARITY, 2026-10-27: --bankroll, --max-stake-dollars and --require-peer-book now match the trader's override exactly (they had drifted to 500/40/off against a live 1000/20/on since 2026-10-26), and --halt-resume-hours 24 simulates the operator who clears a live halt -- without it the walk-forward latched on 2026-02-03, the first day of a crash, and every money figure covered 12 days of a 293-day range. With both, realised_edge_lcb goes -0.251 -> +1.033 and overconfidence_abs 0.01544 -> 0.00252 on an unchanged forecast: those gates were failing on a truncated sample, not on the model. n_halts is 1 over 293 days. Standing operator policy, 2026-10-21: the Sunday retrain ALWAYS installs, so the model keeps absorbing new data. The gates are advisory and the operator reads them; they are not a blocker. Quote sources are Kalshi-only for price VALIDITY rather than measured skill - the Predexon backfill is unbiased but 54x noisier, stamped a minute late, and quantises the deci-cent tail grid to whole cents in ~27% of rows, so a model trained to beat it may not transfer to a book we can trade. It scores worse on the gates and that is accepted. --peer-quote-sources all keeps Polymarket intact: the source filter matches on the bare name and would otherwise discard the gamma backfill, which is a different pipeline, taking every cross_venue row with it.",
